{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,4]],"date-time":"2026-05-04T15:24:30Z","timestamp":1777908270522,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":93,"publisher":"American Astronomical Society","issue":"5","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,25]],"date-time":"2022-04-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1650844800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,25]],"date-time":"2022-04-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1650844800000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/iopscience.iop.org\/info\/page\/text-and-data-mining"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100002923","name":"Consejo Nacional de Investigaciones Cient\u00edficas y T\u00e9cnicas","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["2020-134-APN-DIR"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2020-134-APN-DIR"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100002923","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["iopscience.iop.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["AJ"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n               <jats:p>NGC 4945 harbors one of the nearest active galactic nuclei (AGNs), which allows us to reach high spatial resolution with current observational facilities. The Seyfert 2 nucleus is deeply obscured by an edge-on disk with <jats:italic>A<\/jats:italic>\n                  <jats:sub>\n                     <jats:italic>V<\/jats:italic>\n                  <\/jats:sub> \u223c 14, requiring infrared observations to study circumnuclear structures and the interstellar medium. In this work, we present an imaging and long-slit spectroscopic study of the nuclear region with a spatial resolution of 6.5 pc, based on Flamingos-2 (F2) and T-ReCS data taken at the Gemini South observatory. We report subarcsecond photometric measurements of the nucleus in <jats:italic>J<\/jats:italic>, <jats:italic>H<\/jats:italic>, and <jats:italic>K<\/jats:italic>\n                  <jats:sub>s<\/jats:sub> filters, and at larger apertures. We do not detect nuclear variability. The nuclear spectra confirm that even in the <jats:italic>K<\/jats:italic> band the AGN emission-line features are completely obscured by dust. We detect a circumnuclear disk in the <jats:italic>K<\/jats:italic> band as well as in the mid-infrared <jats:italic>N<\/jats:italic> and <jats:italic>Q<\/jats:italic>\n                  <jats:sub>a<\/jats:sub>bands, with a radial scale length of \u223c120 pc. The disk shows knots mostly in a ring-like arrangement that has been previously detected with Pa<jats:italic>\u03b1<\/jats:italic> observations from the Hubble Space Telescope, indicating that these are deeply embedded, massive young star clusters. We present here the spectrum of one of the brightest unresolved objects (<jats:italic>R<\/jats:italic> &lt; 5 pc), which we identify as a super star cluster candidate with <jats:inline-formula>\n                     <jats:tex-math>\n\n<\/jats:tex-math>\n                     <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" overflow=\"scroll\">\n                        <mml:msub>\n                           <mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mi>M<\/mml:mi>\n                           <\/mml:mrow>\n                           <mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                 <mml:mrow>\n                                    <mml:mi>K<\/mml:mi>\n                                 <\/mml:mrow>\n                                 <mml:mrow>\n                                    <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mml:mi>\n                                 <\/mml:mrow>\n                              <\/mml:msub>\n                           <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msub>\n                        <mml:mspace width=\"0.25em\"\/>\n                        <mml:mo>\u2212<\/mml:mo>\n                        <mml:mn>16.6<\/mml:mn>\n                        <mml:mo>\u00b1<\/mml:mo>\n                        <mml:mn>0.4<\/mml:mn>\n                     <\/mml:math>\n                     <jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" xlink:href=\"ajac5ea4ieqn1.gif\" xlink:type=\"simple\"\/>\n                  <\/jats:inline-formula>. For the circumnuclear region, a detailed rotation curve allows us to measure a nuclear mass of <jats:italic>M<\/jats:italic> = (4.4 \u00b1 3) \u00d7 10<jats:sup>6<\/jats:sup>\n                  <jats:italic>M<\/jats:italic>\n                  <jats:sub>\u2299<\/jats:sub> within a radius of \u223c6.5 pc. We also report the detection of hot dust (\u223c1000 K) out to a nuclear distance of 80 pc measured along the semimajor axis.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3847\/1538-3881\/ac5ea4","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,25]],"date-time":"2022-04-25T10:09:12Z","timestamp":1650881352000},"page":"230","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":5,"title":["An Infrared View of the Obscured AGN Environment in NGC 4945"],"prefix":"10.3847","volume":"163","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9293-4449","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"G.","family":"Gaspar","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9716-5335","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"R. J.","family":"D\u00edaz","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0469-3193","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"D.","family":"Mast","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4450-5655","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"M. P.","family":"Ag\u00fcero","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2568-9994","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"M.","family":"Schirmer","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3501-5360","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"G.","family":"G\u00fcnthardt","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6048-9715","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"E. O.","family":"Schmidt","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"2208","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,25]]},"reference":[{"key":"ajac5ea4bib1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"A104","DOI":"10.1051\/0004-6361\/202038282","volume":"640","author":"Aalto","year":"2020","journal-title":"A&A"},{"key":"ajac5ea4bib2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"164","DOI":"10.1088\/0004-637X\/755\/2\/164","volume":"755","author":"Ackermann","year":"2012","journal-title":"ApJ"},{"key":"ajac5ea4bib3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"219","DOI":"10.4236\/ijaa.2016.63018","volume":"6","author":"Ag\u00fcero","year":"2016","journal-title":"IJAA"},{"key":"ajac5ea4bib4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"196","DOI":"10.1086\/305269","volume":"495","author":"Alonso-Herrero","year":"1998","journal-title":"ApJ"},{"key":"ajac5ea4bib5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"473","DOI":"10.1146\/annurev.aa.31.090193.002353","volume":"31","author":"Antonucci","year":"1993","journal-title":"ARA&A"},{"key":"ajac5ea4bib6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"252","DOI":"10.1093\/mnras\/stw1659","volume":"463","author":"Bendo","year":"2016","journal-title":"MNRAS"},{"key":"ajac5ea4bib7","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"159","DOI":"10.1086\/510708","volume":"657","author":"Bian","year":"2007","journal-title":"ApJ"},{"key":"ajac5ea